<title>DUBAI: U.S. envoy leaves Oman for talks with Iraqi Kurds.</title>
<headline>U.S. envoy leaves Oman for talks with Iraqi Kurds.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Assistant Secretary of State Robert Pelletreau left Oman for Turkey on Monday where he will chair talks between two feuding Iraqi Kurdish groups, the official Oman News Agency said.</p>
<p>Pelletreau, who met Sultan Qaboos during his official trip to the Gulf, also visited the United Arab Emirates.</p>
